OL,3,GNEWSAGraffiti from the past found
OL,4,Aduring restoration
OL,5,
OL,6,FGraffiti dating back more than 250
OL,7,Fyears has been uncovered during
OL,8,Frestoration work in what is thought to
OL,9,Fbe Europe's oldest residential street.
OL,11,FThe markings were discovered on the
OL,12,Froof of a tower at Vicars' Close in
OL,13,FWells, Somerset.
OL,15,FThe homes date back to the 14th Century
OL,16,Fand were built to provide accommodation
OL,17,Fat Wells Cathedral. The graffiti
OL,18,Fincludes initials, decorative patterns
OL,19,Fand the outline of a foot dating back
OL,20,Fto the 1780s.
OL,23,APub: 20-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
FL,349,340,200,160,0,100
